 ],
 "text": "Some people dislike rainy days, but I have learned to enjoy them. Rain changes the sound of the city. The streets become quieter, and the air smells fresh and clean. On a rainy weekend, I make a pot of tea and open a good book. I also take the time for small jobs that I usually avoid. I sort old papers, fix a loose button or clean the windows from inside. When the rain stops, I go for a walk. The light after rain is often beautiful. So the next time it rains, try to see it as a gift of time. Rain, after all, keeps the gardens green."
